.TH CCOL_CHAN_TRY_SEND_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_chan_try_send_zc \- try to send a message with no block
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_chan_try_send_zc(ccol_channel *ch, c_message_t *msg);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function tries to send the message immediately. It uses the queue that
the channel picks itself. If that queue is full, the function returns
immediately.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch   Channel to send through
msg  Message to send. On success the ownership of the data moves to the
     channel.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success         - The function sent the message
ccol_invalid_args    - ch or msg is NULL, or the check of msg fails
ccol_not_permitted   - Sends on the chosen direction are turned off
ccol_container_full  - The chosen queue is full
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The function never blocks.
The function picks the direction itself from the ID of the thread.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_chan_send_zc (3),
.BR ccol_chan_timed_send_zc (3)
